    {
      "text": "pentagonal bipyramid",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Shape of XeF $\\rightarrow$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0016_110f4cff8d86.png\">\r\n\r\nThe Xe show $s p^{3} d^{3}$ -hybridisation in $XeF^{-}_{5}$, Thus, its geometry is Pentagonal-bipyramidal. But, number of electron pair $=\\frac{8+5+1}{2}=7$ Number of bond pair $=5^{2},$ number of lone pair $=2$ A lot of electrons are present at axil position and all bonds are in same plane. Hence, the shape is planar."
  }
}